(window.IND_GITA_V = window.IND_GITA_V || {})[3] = [{"v":1,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":"अर्जुन उवाच","spp":"before","sa":"ज्यायसी चेत्कर्मणस्ते मता बुद्धिर्जनार्दन ।\nतत्किं कर्मणि घोरे मां नियोजयसि केशव ॥","iast":"jyāyasī cetkarmaṇaste matā buddhirjanārdana |\ntatkiṃ karmaṇi ghore māṃ niyojayasi keśava ||","read":"jyaayasee chetkarmanaste mataa buddhirjanaardana |\ntatkim karmani ghore maam niyojayasi keshava ||","spli":"arjuna uvāca","splr":"arjuna uvaacha","en":"Arjuna said: If it be thought by Thee that knowledge is superior to action, O Janârdana, why dost Thou, O Keshava, enjoin on me this terrible action?","en2":"If, O Janârdana, according to Thee, knowledge is superior to action, why then, O Keshava, dost Thou engage me in this terrible action?","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":2,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"व्यामिश्रेणेव वाक्येन बुद्धिं मोहयसीव मे ।\nतदेकं वद निश्चित्य येन श्रेयोऽहमाप्नुयाम् ॥","iast":"vyāmiśreṇeva vākyena buddhiṃ mohayasīva me |\ntadekaṃ vada niścitya yena śreyo’hamāpnuyām ||","read":"vyaamishreneva vaakyena buddhim mohayaseeva me |\ntadekam vada nishchitya yena shreyo'hamaapnuyaam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"With these perplexing words Thou only confusest my understanding; therefore tell me with certainty the one way by which I may reach bliss.","en2":"With these seemingly conflicting words, Thou art, as it were, bewildering my understanding;—tell me that one thing for certain, by which I can attain to the highest.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":3,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":"श्री भगवानुवाच","spp":"before","sa":"लोकेऽस्मिन्द्विविधा निष्ठा पुरा प्रोक्ता मयानघ ।\nज्ञानयोगेन सांख्यानां कर्मयोगेन योगिनाम् ॥","iast":"loke’smindvividhā niṣṭhā purā proktā mayānagha |\njñānayogena sāṃkhyānāṃ karmayogena yoginām ||","read":"loke'smindvividhaa nishthaa puraa proktaa mayaanagha |\njnaanayogena saamkhyaanaam karmayogena yoginaam ||","spli":"śrī bhagavānuvāca","splr":"shree bhagavaanuvaacha","en":"The Blessed Lord said: In this world there is a twofold path, as I before said, O sinless one: that of yoga by knowledge, of the Sâñkhyas; and that of yoga by action, of the Yogis.","en2":"In the beginning (of creation), O sinless one, the twofold path of devotion was given by Me to this world;—the path of knowledge for the meditative, the path of work for the active.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":4,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"न कर्मणामनारम्भान्नैष्कर्म्यं पुरुषोऽश्नुते ।\nन च संन्यसनादेव सिद्धिं समधिगच्छति ॥","iast":"na karmaṇāmanārambhānnaiṣkarmyaṃ puruṣo’śnute |\nna ca saṃnyasanādeva siddhiṃ samadhigacchati ||","read":"na karmanaamanaarambhaannaishkarmyam purusho'shnute |\nna cha samnyasanaadeva siddhim samadhigachchhati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Man winneth not freedom from action by abstaining from activity, nor by mere renunciation doth he rise to perfection.","en2":"By non-performance of work none reaches worklessness; by merely giving up action no one attains to perfection.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":5,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"न हि कश्चित्क्षणमपि जातु तिष्ठत्यकर्मकृत् ।\nकार्यते ह्यवशः कर्म सर्वः प्रकृतिजैर्गुणैः ॥","iast":"na hi kaścitkṣaṇamapi jātu tiṣṭhatyakarmakṛt |\nkāryate hyavaśaḥ karma sarvaḥ prakṛtijairguṇaiḥ ||","read":"na hi kashchitkshanamapi jaatu tishthatyakarmakrit |\nkaaryate hyavashah karma sarvah prakritijairgunaih ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Nor can anyone, even for an instant, remain really actionless; for helplessly is everyone driven to action by the qualities born of nature.","en2":"Verily none can ever rest for even an instant, without performing action; for all are made to act, helplessly indeed, by the Gunas, born of Prakriti.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":6,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"कर्मेन्द्रियाणि संयम्य य आस्ते मनसा स्मरन् ।\nइन्द्रियार्थान्विमूढात्मा मिथ्याचारः स उच्यते ॥","iast":"karmendriyāṇi saṃyamya ya āste manasā smaran |\nindriyārthānvimūḍhātmā mithyācāraḥ sa ucyate ||","read":"karmendriyaani samyamya ya aaste manasaa smaran |\nindriyaarthaanvimoodhaatmaa mithyaachaarah sa uchyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Who sitteth, controlling the organs of action, but dwelling in his mind on the objects of the senses, that bewildered man is called a hypocrite.","en2":"He, who restraining the organs of action, sits revolving in the mind, thoughts regarding objects of senses, he, of deluded understanding, is called a hypocrite.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":7,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यस्त्विन्द्रियाणि मनसा नियम्यारभतेऽर्जुन ।\nकर्मेन्द्रियैः कर्मयोगमसक्तः स विशिष्यते ॥","iast":"yastvindriyāṇi manasā niyamyārabhate’rjuna |\nkarmendriyaiḥ karmayogamasaktaḥ sa viśiṣyate ||","read":"yastvindriyaani manasaa niyamyaarabhate'rjuna |\nkarmendriyaih karmayogamasaktah sa vishishyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"But who, controlling the senses by the mind, O Arjuna, with the organs of action without attachment, performeth yoga by action, he is worthy.","en2":"But, who, controlling the senses by the mind, unattached, directs his organs of action to the path of work, he, O Arjuna, excels.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":8,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"नियतं कुरु कर्म त्वं कर्म ज्यायो ह्यकर्मणः ।\nशरीरयात्रापि च ते न प्रसिद्ध्येदकर्मणः ॥","iast":"niyataṃ kuru karma tvaṃ karma jyāyo hyakarmaṇaḥ |\nśarīrayātrāpi ca te na prasiddhyedakarmaṇaḥ ||","read":"niyatam kuru karma tvam karma jyaayo hyakarmanah |\nshareerayaatraapi cha te na prasiddhyedakarmanah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Perform thou right action, for, action is superior to inaction, and, inactive, even the maintenance of thy body would not be possible.","en2":"Do thou perform obligatory action; for action is superior to inaction, and even the bare maintenance of thy body would not be possible if thou art inactive.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":9,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यज्ञार्थात्कर्मणोऽन्यत्र लोकोऽयं कर्मबन्धनः ।\nतदर्थं कर्म कौन्तेय मुक्तसंगः समाचर ॥","iast":"yajñārthātkarmaṇo’nyatra loko’yaṃ karmabandhanaḥ |\ntadarthaṃ karma kaunteya muktasaṃgaḥ samācara ||","read":"yajnaarthaatkarmano'nyatra loko'yam karmabandhanah |\ntadartham karma kaunteya muktasamgah samaachara ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The world is bound by action, unless performed for the sake of sacrifice; for that sake, free from attachment, O son of Kuntî, perform thou action.","en2":"The world is bound by actions other than those performed for the sake of Yajna; do thou therefore, O son of Kunti, perform action for Yajna alone, devoid of attachment.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":10,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सहयज्ञाः प्रजाः सृष्ट्वा पुरोवाच प्रजापतिः ।\nअनेन प्रसविष्यध्वमेष वोऽस्त्विष्टकामधुक् ॥","iast":"sahayajñāḥ prajāḥ sṛṣṭvā purovāca prajāpatiḥ |\nanena prasaviṣyadhvameṣa vo’stviṣṭakāmadhuk ||","read":"sahayajnaah prajaah srishtvaa purovaacha prajaapatih |\nanena prasavishyadhvamesha vo'stvishtakaamadhuk ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Having in ancient times emanated mankind together with sacrifice, the Lord of emanation said: \"By this shall ye propagate; be this to you the giver of desire;","en2":"The Prajâpati, having in the beginning created mankind together with Yajna, said,—\"By this shall ye multiply: this shall be the milch cow of your desires.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":11,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"देवान्भावयतानेन ते देवा भावयन्तु वः ।\nपरस्परं भावयन्तः श्रेयः परमवाप्स्यथ ॥","iast":"devānbhāvayatānena te devā bhāvayantu vaḥ |\nparasparaṃ bhāvayantaḥ śreyaḥ paramavāpsyatha ||","read":"devaanbhaavayataanena te devaa bhaavayantu vah |\nparasparam bhaavayantah shreyah paramavaapsyatha ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"\"With this nourish ye the Shining Ones, and may the Shining Ones nourish you; thus nourishing one another ye shall reap the supremest good.","en2":"\"Cherish the Devas with this, and may those Devas cherish you: thus cherishing one another, ye shall gain the highest good.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":12,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"इष्टान्भोगान्हि वो देवा दास्यन्ते यज्ञभाविताः ।\nतैर्दत्तानप्रदायैभ्यो यो भुङ्क्ते स्तेन एव सः ॥","iast":"iṣṭānbhogānhi vo devā dāsyante yajñabhāvitāḥ |\ntairdattānapradāyaibhyo yo bhuṅkte stena eva saḥ ||","read":"ishtaanbhogaanhi vo devaa daasyante yajnabhaavitaah |\ntairdattaanapradaayaibhyo yo bhunkte stena eva sah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"\"For, nourished by sacrifice, the Shining Ones shall bestow on you the enjoyments you desire.\" A thief verily is he who enjoyeth what is given by Them without returning Them aught.","en2":"\"The Devas, cherished by Yajna, will give you desired-for objects.\" So, he who enjoys objects given by the Devas without offering (in return) to them, is verily a thief.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":13,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यज्ञशिष्टाशिनः सन्तो मुच्यन्ते सर्वकिल्बिषैः ।\nभुञ्जते ते त्वघं पापा ये पचन्त्यात्मकारणात् ॥","iast":"yajñaśiṣṭāśinaḥ santo mucyante sarvakilbiṣaiḥ |\nbhuñjate te tvaghaṃ pāpā ye pacantyātmakāraṇāt ||","read":"yajnashishtaashinah santo muchyante sarvakilbishaih |\nbhunjate te tvagham paapaa ye pachantyaatmakaaranaat ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The righteous, who eat the remains of the sacrifice, are freed from all sins; but the impious, who dress food for their own sakes, they verily eat sin.","en2":"The good, eating the remnants of Yajna, are freed from all sins: but who cook food (only) for themselves, those sinful ones eat sin.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":14,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अन्नाद्भवन्ति भूतानि पर्जन्यादन्नसम्भवः ।\nयज्ञाद्भवति पर्जन्यो यज्ञः कर्मसमुद्भवः ॥","iast":"annādbhavanti bhūtāni parjanyādannasambhavaḥ |\nyajñādbhavati parjanyo yajñaḥ karmasamudbhavaḥ ||","read":"annaadbhavanti bhootaani parjanyaadannasambhavah |\nyajnaadbhavati parjanyo yajnah karmasamudbhavah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"From food creatures become; from rain is the production of food; rain proceedeth from sacrifice; sacrifice ariseth out of action.","en2":"From food come forth beings: from rain food is produced: from Yajna arises rain and Yajna is born of Karma.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":15,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"कर्म ब्रह्मोद्भवं विद्धि ब्रह्माक्षरसमुद्भवम् ।\nतस्मात्सर्वगतं ब्रह्म नित्यं यज्ञे प्रतिष्ठितम् ॥","iast":"karma brahmodbhavaṃ viddhi brahmākṣarasamudbhavam |\ntasmātsarvagataṃ brahma nityaṃ yajñe pratiṣṭhitam ||","read":"karma brahmodbhavam viddhi brahmaaksharasamudbhavam |\ntasmaatsarvagatam brahma nityam yajne pratishthitam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Know thou that from Brahma action groweth, and Brahma from the Imperishable cometh. Therefore the Eternal, the all-permeating, is ever present in sacrifice.","en2":"Know Karma to have risen from the Veda, and the Veda from the Imperishable. Therefore the all-pervading Veda is ever centred in Yajna.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":16,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"एवं प्रवर्तितं चक्रं नानुवर्तयतीह यः ।\nअघायुरिन्द्रियारामो मोघं पार्थ स जीवति ॥","iast":"evaṃ pravartitaṃ cakraṃ nānuvartayatīha yaḥ |\naghāyurindriyārāmo moghaṃ pārtha sa jīvati ||","read":"evam pravartitam chakram naanuvartayateeha yah |\naghaayurindriyaaraamo mogham paartha sa jeevati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who on earth doth not follow the wheel thus revolving, sinful of life and rejoicing in the senses, he, O son of Pritha, liveth in vain.","en2":"He, who here follows not the wheel thus set revolving, living in sin, and satisfied in the senses, O son of Prithâ,—he lives in vain.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":17,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यस्त्वात्मरतिरेव स्यादात्मतृप्तश्च मानवः ।\nआत्मन्येव च सन्तुष्टस्तस्य कार्यं न विद्यते ॥","iast":"yastvātmaratireva syādātmatṛptaśca mānavaḥ |\nātmanyeva ca santuṣṭastasya kāryaṃ na vidyate ||","read":"yastvaatmaratireva syaadaatmatriptashcha maanavah |\naatmanyeva cha santushtastasya kaaryam na vidyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"But the man who rejoiceth in the Self, with the Self is satisfied, and is content in the Self, for him verily there is nothing to do;","en2":"But the man who is devoted to the Self, and is satisfied with the Self, and content in the Self alone, he has no obligatory duty.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":18,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"नैव तस्य कृतेनार्थो नाकृतेनेह कश्चन ।\nन चास्य सर्वभूतेषु कश्चिदर्थव्यपाश्रयः ॥","iast":"naiva tasya kṛtenārtho nākṛteneha kaścana |\nna cāsya sarvabhūteṣu kaścidarthavyapāśrayaḥ ||","read":"naiva tasya kritenaartho naakriteneha kashchana |\nna chaasya sarvabhooteshu kashchidarthavyapaashrayah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"For him there is no interest in things done, in this world, nor any in things not done, nor doth any object of his depend on any being.","en2":"He has no object in this world (to gain) by doing (an action), nor (does he incur any loss) by non-performance of action,—nor has he (need of) depending on any being for any object.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":19,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तस्मादसक्तः सततं कार्यं कर्म समाचर ।\nअसक्तो ह्याचरन्कर्म परमाप्नोति पूरुषः ॥","iast":"tasmādasaktaḥ satataṃ kāryaṃ karma samācara |\nasakto hyācarankarma paramāpnoti pūruṣaḥ ||","read":"tasmaadasaktah satatam kaaryam karma samaachara |\nasakto hyaacharankarma paramaapnoti poorushah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Therefore, without attachment, constantly perform action which is duty, for, by performing action without attachment, man verily reacheth the Supreme.","en2":"Therefore, do thou always perform actions which are obligatory, without attachment;—by performing action without attachment, one attains to the highest.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":20,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"कर्मणैव हि संसिद्धिमास्थिता जनकादयः ।\nलोकसंग्रहमेवापि संपश्यन्कर्तुमर्हसि ॥","iast":"karmaṇaiva hi saṃsiddhimāsthitā janakādayaḥ |\nlokasaṃgrahamevāpi saṃpaśyankartumarhasi ||","read":"karmanaiva hi samsiddhimaasthitaa janakaadayah |\nlokasamgrahamevaapi sampashyankartumarhasi ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Janaka and others indeed attained to perfection by action: then having an eye to the welfare of he world also, thou shouldst perform action.","en2":"Verily by action alone, Janaka and others attained perfection;—also, simply with the view for the guidance of men, thou shouldst perform action.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":21,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यद्यदाचरति श्रेष्ठस्तत्तदेवेतरो जनः ।\nस यत्प्रमाणं कुरुते लोकस्तदनुवर्तते ॥","iast":"yadyadācarati śreṣṭhastattadevetaro janaḥ |\nsa yatpramāṇaṃ kurute lokastadanuvartate ||","read":"yadyadaacharati shreshthastattadevetaro janah |\nsa yatpramaanam kurute lokastadanuvartate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Whatsoever a great man doeth, that other men also do; the standard he setteth up, by that the people go.","en2":"Whatsoever the superior person does, that is followed by others. What he demonstrates by action, that, people follow.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":22,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"न मे पार्थास्ति कर्तव्यं त्रिषु लोकेषु किञ्चन ।\nनानवाप्तमवाप्तव्यं वर्त एव च कर्मणि ॥","iast":"na me pārthāsti kartavyaṃ triṣu lokeṣu kiñcana |\nnānavāptamavāptavyaṃ varta eva ca karmaṇi ||","read":"na me paarthaasti kartavyam trishu lokeshu kinchana |\nnaanavaaptamavaaptavyam varta eva cha karmani ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"There is nothing in the three worlds, O Pârtha, that should be done by Me, nor anything unattained that might be attained; yet I mingle in action.","en2":"I have, O son of Prithâ, no duty, nothing that I have not gained, and nothing that I have to gain, in the three worlds; yet, I continue in action.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":23,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यदि ह्यहं न वर्तेयं जातु कर्मण्यतन्द्रितः ।\nमम वर्त्मानुवर्तन्ते मनुष्याः पार्थ सर्वशः ॥","iast":"yadi hyahaṃ na varteyaṃ jātu karmaṇyatandritaḥ |\nmama vartmānuvartante manuṣyāḥ pārtha sarvaśaḥ ||","read":"yadi hyaham na varteyam jaatu karmanyatandritah |\nmama vartmaanuvartante manushyaah paartha sarvashah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"For if I mingled not ever in action unwearied, men all around would follow My path, O son of Prithâ.","en2":"If ever I did not continue in work, without relaxation, men, O son of Prithâ, would in every way, follow in My wake.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":24,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"उत्सीदेयुरिमे लोका न कुर्यां कर्म चेदहम् ।\nसङ्करस्य च कर्ता स्यामुपहन्यामिमाः प्रजाः ॥","iast":"utsīdeyurime lokā na kuryāṃ karma cedaham |\nsaṅkarasya ca kartā syāmupahanyāmimāḥ prajāḥ ||","read":"utseedeyurime lokaa na kuryaam karma chedaham |\nsankarasya cha kartaa syaamupahanyaamimaah prajaah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"These worlds would fall into ruin, if I did not perform action; I should be the author of confusion of castes, and should destroy these creatures.","en2":"If I did not do work, these worlds would perish. I should be the cause of the admixture of races, and I should ruin these beings.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":25,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सक्ताः कर्मण्यविद्वांसो यथा कुर्वन्ति भारत ।\nकुर्याद्विद्वांस्तथासक्तश्चिकीर्षुर्लोकसंग्रहम् ॥","iast":"saktāḥ karmaṇyavidvāṃso yathā kurvanti bhārata |\nkuryādvidvāṃstathāsaktaścikīrṣurlokasaṃgraham ||","read":"saktaah karmanyavidvaamso yathaa kurvanti bhaarata |\nkuryaadvidvaamstathaasaktashchikeershurlokasamgraham ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"As the ignorant act from attachment to action, O Bhârata, so should the wise act without attachment, desiring the welfare of the world.","en2":"As do the unwise, attached to work, act, so should the wise act, O descendant of Bharata, (but) without attachment, desirous of the guidance of the world.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":26,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"न बुद्धिभेदं जनयेदज्ञानां कर्मसङ्गिनाम् ।\nजोषयेत्सर्वकर्माणि विद्वान् युक्तः समाचरन् ॥","iast":"na buddhibhedaṃ janayedajñānāṃ karmasaṅginām |\njoṣayetsarvakarmāṇi vidvān yuktaḥ samācaran ||","read":"na buddhibhedam janayedajnaanaam karmasanginaam |\njoshayetsarvakarmaani vidvaan yuktah samaacharan ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Let no wise man unsettle the mind of ignorant people attached to action; but acting in harmony with Me let him render all action attractive.","en2":"One should not unsettle the understanding of the ignorant, attached to action; the wise, (himself) steadily acting, should engage (the ignorant) in all work.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":27,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"प्रकृतेः क्रियमाणानि गुणैः कर्माणि सर्वशः ।\nअहङ्कारविमूढात्मा कर्ताऽहमिति मन्यते ॥","iast":"prakṛteḥ kriyamāṇāni guṇaiḥ karmāṇi sarvaśaḥ |\nahaṅkāravimūḍhātmā kartā’hamiti manyate ||","read":"prakriteh kriyamaanaani gunaih karmaani sarvashah |\nahankaaravimoodhaatmaa kartaa'hamiti manyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"All actions are wrought by the quali ties of nature only. The self, deluded by egoism, thinketh: \"I am the doer.\"","en2":"The Gunas of Prakriti perform all action. With the understanding deluded by egoism, man thinks, \"I am the doer.\"","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":28,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तत्त्ववित्तु महाबाहो गुणकर्मविभागयोः ।\nगुणा गुणेषु वर्तन्त इति मत्वा न सज्जते ॥","iast":"tattvavittu mahābāho guṇakarmavibhāgayoḥ |\nguṇā guṇeṣu vartanta iti matvā na sajjate ||","read":"tattvavittu mahaabaaho gunakarmavibhaagayoh |\ngunaa guneshu vartanta iti matvaa na sajjate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"But he, O mighty-armed, who knoweth the essence of the divisions of the qualities and functions, holding that \"the qualities move amid the qualities,\" is not attached.","en2":"But, one, with true insight into the domains of Guna and Karma, knowing that Gunas as senses merely rest on Gunas as objects, does not become attached.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":29,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"प्रकृतेर्गुणसम्मूढाः सज्जन्ते गुणकर्मसु ।\nतानकृत्स्नविदो मन्दान्कृत्स्नविन्न विचालयेत् ॥","iast":"prakṛterguṇasammūḍhāḥ sajjante guṇakarmasu |\ntānakṛtsnavido mandānkṛtsnavinna vicālayet ||","read":"prakritergunasammoodhaah sajjante gunakarmasu |\ntaanakritsnavido mandaankritsnavinna vichaalayet ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Those deluded by the qualities of nature are attached to the functions of the qualities. The man of perfect knowledge should not unsettle the foolish whose knowledge is imperfect.","en2":"Men of perfect knowledge should not unsettle (the understanding of) people of dull wit and imperfect knowledge, who deluded by the Gunas of Prakriti attach (themselves) to the functions of the Gunas.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":30,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"मयि सर्वाणि कर्माणि संन्यस्याध्यात्मचेतसा ।\nनिराशीर्निर्ममो भूत्वा युध्यस्व विगतज्वरः ॥","iast":"mayi sarvāṇi karmāṇi saṃnyasyādhyātmacetasā |\nnirāśīrnirmamo bhūtvā yudhyasva vigatajvaraḥ ||","read":"mayi sarvaani karmaani samnyasyaadhyaatmachetasaa |\nniraasheernirmamo bhootvaa yudhyasva vigatajvarah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Surrendering all actions to Me, with thy thoughts resting on the supreme Self, from hope and egoism freed, and of mental fever cured, engage in battle.","en2":"Renouncing all actions to Me, with mind centred on the Self, getting rid of hope and selfishness, fight,—free from (mental) fever.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":31,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ये मे मतमिदं नित्यमनुतिष्ठन्ति मानवाः ।\nश्रद्धावन्तोऽनसूयन्तो मुच्यन्ते तेऽपि कर्मभिः ॥","iast":"ye me matamidaṃ nityamanutiṣṭhanti mānavāḥ |\nśraddhāvanto’nasūyanto mucyante te’pi karmabhiḥ ||","read":"ye me matamidam nityamanutishthanti maanavaah |\nshraddhaavanto'nasooyanto muchyante te'pi karmabhih ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Who abide ever in this teaching of Mine full of faith and free from caviling, they too are released from actions.","en2":"Those men who constantly practise this teaching of Mine, full of Shraddhâ and without cavilling, they too, are freed from work.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":32,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ये त्वेतदभ्यसूयन्तो नानुतिष्ठन्ति मे मतम् ।\nसर्वज्ञानविमूढांस्तान्विद्धि नष्टानचेतसः ॥","iast":"ye tvetadabhyasūyanto nānutiṣṭhanti me matam |\nsarvajñānavimūḍhāṃstānviddhi naṣṭānacetasaḥ ||","read":"ye tvetadabhyasooyanto naanutishthanti me matam |\nsarvajnaanavimoodhaamstaanviddhi nashtaanachetasah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Who carp at My teaching and act not thereon, senseless, deluded in all knowledge, know thou these mindless ones as fated to be destroyed.","en2":"But those who decrying this teaching of Mine do not practise (it), deluded in all knowledge, and devoid of discrimination, know them to be ruined.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":33,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सदृशं चेष्टते स्वस्याः प्रकृतेर्ज्ञानवानपि ।\nप्रकृतिं यान्ति भूतानि निग्रहः किं करिष्यति ॥","iast":"sadṛśaṃ ceṣṭate svasyāḥ prakṛterjñānavānapi |\nprakṛtiṃ yānti bhūtāni nigrahaḥ kiṃ kariṣyati ||","read":"sadrisham cheshtate svasyaah prakriterjnaanavaanapi |\nprakritim yaanti bhootaani nigrahah kim karishyati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Even the man of knowledge behaves in conformity with his own nature; beings follow nature; what shall restraint avail?","en2":"Even a wise man acts in accordance with his own nature: beings follow nature: what can restraint do?","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":34,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"इन्द्रियस्येन्द्रियस्यार्थे रागद्वेषौ व्यवस्थितौ ।\nतयोर्न वशमागच्छेत्तौ ह्यस्य परिपन्थिनौ ॥","iast":"indriyasyendriyasyārthe rāgadveṣau vyavasthitau |\ntayorna vaśamāgacchettau hyasya paripanthinau ||","read":"indriyasyendriyasyaarthe raagadveshau vyavasthitau |\ntayorna vashamaagachchhettau hyasya paripanthinau ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Affection and aversion for the objects of sense abide in the senses; let none come under the dominion of these two; they are obstructors of the path.","en2":"Attachment and aversion of the senses for their respective objects are natural: let none come under their sway: they are his foes.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":35,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"श्रेयान्स्वधर्मो विगुणः परधर्मात्स्वनुष्ठितात् ।\nस्वधर्मे निधनं श्रेयः परधर्मो भयावहः ॥","iast":"śreyānsvadharmo viguṇaḥ paradharmātsvanuṣṭhitāt |\nsvadharme nidhanaṃ śreyaḥ paradharmo bhayāvahaḥ ||","read":"shreyaansvadharmo vigunah paradharmaatsvanushthitaat |\nsvadharme nidhanam shreyah paradharmo bhayaavahah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Better one's own duty, though destitute of merit, than the duty of another, well discharged. Better death in the discharge of one's own duty; the duty of another is full of danger.","en2":"Better is one's own Dharma, (though) imperfect, than the Dharma of another well-performed. Better is death in one's own Dharma: the Dharma of another is fraught with fear.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":36,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":"अर्जुन उवाच","spp":"before","sa":"अथ केन प्रयुक्तोऽयं पापं चरति पूरुषः ।\nअनिच्छन्नपि वार्ष्णेय बलादिव नियोजितः ॥","iast":"atha kena prayukto’yaṃ pāpaṃ carati pūruṣaḥ |\nanicchannapi vārṣṇeya balādiva niyojitaḥ ||","read":"atha kena prayukto'yam paapam charati poorushah |\nanichchhannapi vaarshneya balaadiva niyojitah ||","spli":"arjuna uvāca","splr":"arjuna uvaacha","en":"Arjuna said: But dragged on by what does a man commit sin, reluctantly indeed, O Varshneya, as it were by force constrained?","en2":"But by what impelled does man commit sin, though against his wishes, O Vârshneya, constrained as it were, by force?","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":37,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":"श्री भगवानुवाच","spp":"before","sa":"काम एष क्रोध एष रजोगुणसमुद्भवः ।\nमहाशनो महापाप्मा विद्ध्येनमिह वैरिणम् ॥","iast":"kāma eṣa krodha eṣa rajoguṇasamudbhavaḥ |\nmahāśano mahāpāpmā viddhyenamiha vairiṇam ||","read":"kaama esha krodha esha rajogunasamudbhavah |\nmahaashano mahaapaapmaa viddhyenamiha vairinam ||","spli":"śrī bhagavānuvāca","splr":"shree bhagavaanuvaacha","en":"The Blessed Lord said: It is desire, it is wrath, begotten by the quality of motion; all-consuming, all-polluting, know thou this as our foe here on earth.","en2":"It is desire—it is anger, born of the Rajo-guna: of great craving, and of great sin; know this as the foe here (in this world).","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":38,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"धूमेनाव्रियते वह्निर्यथाऽऽदर्शो मलेन च ।\nयथोल्बेनावृतो गर्भस्तथा तेनेदमावृतम् ॥","iast":"dhūmenāvriyate vahniryathā’’darśo malena ca |\nyatholbenāvṛto garbhastathā tenedamāvṛtam ||","read":"dhoomenaavriyate vahniryathaa''darsho malena cha |\nyatholbenaavrito garbhastathaa tenedamaavritam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"As a flame is enveloped by smoke, as a mirror by dust, as an embryo is wrapped by the amnion, so This is enveloped by it.","en2":"As fire is enveloped by smoke, as a mirror by dust, as an embryo by the secundine, so is it covered by that.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":39,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"आवृतं ज्ञानमेतेन ज्ञानिनो नित्यवैरिणा ।\nकामरूपेण कौन्तेय दुष्पूरेणानलेन च ॥","iast":"āvṛtaṃ jñānametena jñānino nityavairiṇā |\nkāmarūpeṇa kaunteya duṣpūreṇānalena ca ||","read":"aavritam jnaanametena jnaanino nityavairinaa |\nkaamaroopena kaunteya dushpoorenaanalena cha ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Enveloped is wisdom by this constant enemy of the wise in the form of desire, which is insatiable as a flame.","en2":"Knowledge is covered by this, the constant foe of the wise, O son of Kunti, the unappeasable fire of desire.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":40,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"इन्द्रियाणि मनो बुद्धिरस्याधिष्ठानमुच्यते ।\nएतैर्विमोहयत्येष ज्ञानमावृत्य देहिनम् ॥","iast":"indriyāṇi mano buddhirasyādhiṣṭhānamucyate |\netairvimohayatyeṣa jñānamāvṛtya dehinam ||","read":"indriyaani mano buddhirasyaadhishthaanamuchyate |\netairvimohayatyesha jnaanamaavritya dehinam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The senses, the mind and the Reason are said to be its seat; by these enveloping wisdom, it bewilders the dweller in the body.","en2":"The senses, the mind and the intellect are said to be its abode: through these, it deludes the embodied by veiling his wisdom.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":41,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तस्मात्त्वमिन्द्रियाण्यादौ नियम्य भरतर्षभ ।\nपाप्मानं प्रजहि ह्येनं ज्ञानविज्ञाननाशनम् ॥","iast":"tasmāttvamindriyāṇyādau niyamya bharatarṣabha |\npāpmānaṃ prajahi hyenaṃ jñānavijñānanāśanam ||","read":"tasmaattvamindriyaanyaadau niyamya bharatarshabha |\npaapmaanam prajahi hyenam jnaanavijnaananaashanam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Therefore, O best of the Bhâratas, mastering first the senses, do thou slay this thing of sin, destructive of wisdom and knowledge.","en2":"Therefore, O Bull of the Bharata race, controlling the senses at the outset, kill it,—the sinful, the destroyer of knowledge and realisation.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":42,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"इन्द्रियाणि पराण्याहुरिन्द्रियेभ्यः परं मनः ।\nमनसस्तु परा बुद्धिर्यो बुद्धेः परतस्तु सः ॥","iast":"indriyāṇi parāṇyāhurindriyebhyaḥ paraṃ manaḥ |\nmanasastu parā buddhiryo buddheḥ paratastu saḥ ||","read":"indriyaani paraanyaahurindriyebhyah param manah |\nmanasastu paraa buddhiryo buddheh paratastu sah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"It is said that the senses are great; greater than the senses is the mind: greater than the mind is the Reason; but what is greater than the Reason, is He.","en2":"The senses are said to be superior (to the body); the mind is superior to the senses; the intellect is superior to the mind; and that which is superior to the intellect is He (the Atman).","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":43,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"एवं बुद्धेः परं बुद्ध्वा संस्तभ्यात्मानमात्मना ।\nजहि शत्रुं महाबाहो कामरूपं दुरासदम् ॥","iast":"evaṃ buddheḥ paraṃ buddhvā saṃstabhyātmānamātmanā |\njahi śatruṃ mahābāho kāmarūpaṃ durāsadam ||","read":"evam buddheh param buddhvaa samstabhyaatmaanamaatmanaa |\njahi shatrum mahaabaaho kaamaroopam duraasadam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Thus understanding Him as greater than the Reason, restraining the self by the Self, slay thou, O mighty-armed, the enemy in the form of desire, difficult to overcome.","en2":"Thus, knowing Him who is superior to the intellect, and restraining the self by the Self, destroy, O mighty-armed, that enemy, the unseizable foe, desire.","en2r":null,"rv":null}];
